WEBVTT

01:40.642 --> 01:42.685
When did you last replace your shaft?

01:42.936 --> 01:45.772
Six days ago, after the mop-up operation.

01:46.815 --> 01:47.857
The records confirm.

01:48.441 --> 01:50.110
All right. You're next.

01:50.652 --> 01:53.571
I'm Christa Lenz of the 42nd Squad!

01:53.988 --> 01:55.365
Equipment check.

01:55.990 --> 01:58.952
So killing Titans
can actually get you in trouble?

01:59.994 --> 02:01.121
Yes, it's crazy,

02:01.204 --> 02:02.664
but they were valuable test subjects.

02:02.747 --> 02:06.918
Even so, why are they searching
for the culprits among us cadets?

02:07.001 --> 02:11.214
We're worn out enough as it is,
cleaning up the battlefield all the time.

02:13.550 --> 02:16.261
Whoever it was really hated Titans.

02:16.386 --> 02:17.220
Yes.

02:17.345 --> 02:20.557
But they pretty much helped the Titans,
if anything.

02:21.516 --> 02:24.644
Maybe it helped quench their thirst
for revenge,

02:24.978 --> 02:26.813
but it was also a big setback
for humanity.

02:27.605 --> 02:30.483
I'm not too bright,
so I think I can relate.

02:31.234 --> 02:35.822
Before I actually saw a Titan,
I planned on joining the Scouts.

02:37.198 --> 02:38.867
Now I never want to see another one again.

02:39.868 --> 02:42.579
But today is the day we have to pick
a regiment to join.

02:50.545 --> 02:53.089
Is Jean seriously going to...

03:07.270 --> 03:09.522
Everyone is having regrets.

03:11.024 --> 03:12.775
They never would have chosen
to be soldiers

03:13.318 --> 03:14.903
if they knew this hell awaited them.

03:16.321 --> 03:18.197
Now that they're utterly drained,

03:18.948 --> 03:20.867
that's the only thing
they can think about.

03:31.252 --> 03:32.337
Marco.

03:33.338 --> 03:36.424
I don't know
which bones are yours anymore.

03:42.513 --> 03:44.224
If I hadn't become a soldier,

03:45.183 --> 03:48.061
I never would have had to worry
about who's next.

03:50.813 --> 03:53.858
Are we just going to throw away
all the advances in techniques

03:53.942 --> 03:56.444
that cost us tens of thousands of lives,
so we can be the Titans' food?

03:57.195 --> 04:00.531
I know I have to fight.

04:01.532 --> 04:06.037
But not everyone can be
a suicidal maniac like you.

04:12.252 --> 04:14.379
I don't mean any offense by this,

04:15.421 --> 04:17.340
but I think the fact
that you aren't strong

04:17.924 --> 04:20.343
really lets you understand
how the weak feel.

04:20.885 --> 04:25.348
And your skill at recognizing
a situation as it unfolds

04:25.598 --> 04:28.518
gives you a clear grasp of
what needs to be done now, you know?

04:36.192 --> 04:38.945
What needs to be done now?

04:40.947 --> 04:42.573
Hey, guys.

04:46.202 --> 04:49.831
Have you decided
which regiment you're going to join?

04:51.541 --> 04:52.875
I have.

04:54.085 --> 04:55.211
I'm...

04:56.462 --> 04:57.505
I'm...

04:59.257 --> 05:00.842
going to join the Scout Regiment!

05:11.894 --> 05:12.812
Damn it.

05:13.438 --> 05:15.857
Hey, Annie. What do you think?

05:16.274 --> 05:18.860
Jean says he's going to join
the Scout Regiment.

05:18.943 --> 05:20.570
What? Jean is?

05:20.778 --> 05:21.738
I don't really care.

05:22.280 --> 05:24.032
Yes, you're joining
the Military Police Regiment.

05:24.574 --> 05:26.659
Maybe I should too after all?

05:28.536 --> 05:29.620
Tell me.

05:29.704 --> 05:32.040
If someone told you to die, would you?

05:32.623 --> 05:33.791
What?

05:33.875 --> 05:35.043
No.

05:35.418 --> 05:38.504
Then do what matters most to you.

05:40.256 --> 05:42.091
What about you, Armin?

05:42.175 --> 05:43.009
What?

05:43.718 --> 05:44.635
I...

05:45.178 --> 05:47.305
I think I might

05:47.764 --> 05:50.266
if the situation called for it
and I understood the reason why.

05:50.933 --> 05:52.185
Not that I would want to.

05:52.435 --> 05:53.352
I see.

05:53.436 --> 05:54.353
So you've decided.

05:54.729 --> 05:55.563
Yes.

05:56.230 --> 05:58.649
Although it has always been
my plan anyway.

05:58.941 --> 06:01.402
Oh, man. Not you too, Armin?

06:03.237 --> 06:06.324
You're weak, but you have guts.

06:06.657 --> 06:08.493
Thanks.

06:09.368 --> 06:12.789
You know,
you're actually pretty nice, Annie.

06:12.872 --> 06:13.790
What?

06:14.207 --> 06:18.419
I mean, you seem apprehensive
about us joining the Scouting Regiment.

06:18.961 --> 06:20.546
Plus, I assume you have a reason

06:20.880 --> 06:22.799
for joining
the Military Police Regiment, right?

06:23.633 --> 06:24.759
Not really.

06:26.302 --> 06:30.807
I just want to stay alive.

06:38.481 --> 06:40.233
In the end, it seems they never found

06:40.316 --> 06:43.611
whoever used the omnidirectional mobility
gear without permission.

06:44.112 --> 06:46.697
- Who could it be?
- Who knows?

06:47.073 --> 06:50.118
Right now, I'm more worried about
the upcoming rookie solicitation.

06:50.827 --> 06:54.372
How many rookies will be willing
to join us just for the hell of it?

06:55.456 --> 06:56.624
Hey, Eren.

06:56.999 --> 06:59.752
Is there anyone in your class
who's thinking of joining us?

07:00.253 --> 07:01.295
There are.

07:02.797 --> 07:04.841
Well, there were.

07:06.050 --> 07:07.718
I'm not sure about it now.

07:09.137 --> 07:10.138
Assemble!

07:14.142 --> 07:16.269
Get ready at once! We're going on patrol!

07:16.352 --> 07:17.270
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

07:17.520 --> 07:19.772
Good morning, Captain Levi!

07:19.939 --> 07:20.982
Listen, Eren.

07:21.065 --> 07:23.025
Don't fall more than two lengths behind.

07:23.401 --> 07:26.320
You're only allowed to wander around
because I'm watching you.

07:26.404 --> 07:27.697
Don't forget that.

07:27.780 --> 07:28.698
Yes, sir!

07:28.781 --> 07:29.657
Let's go!

08:00.188 --> 08:01.189
Jean!

08:02.023 --> 08:03.983
Are you really joining the Scout Regiment?

08:04.233 --> 08:05.109
Yes.

08:05.276 --> 08:06.652
Why the sudden change of heart?

08:06.736 --> 08:09.780
I mean, aren't you afraid?

08:09.864 --> 08:10.740
What?

08:10.823 --> 08:13.201
Of course,
I'm afraid of joining the Scout Regiment.

08:13.284 --> 08:15.369
What? Then why are you...

08:15.453 --> 08:18.998
It's not because I'm not scared
of the Titans or anything like that.

08:19.790 --> 08:25.505
Nor am I going to say that capable people
should join the Scout Regiment.

08:26.297 --> 08:28.382
I'm not like that suicidal maniac.

08:29.175 --> 08:30.259
Eren?

08:31.093 --> 08:33.930
He's already been a Scout for a while now.

08:34.430 --> 08:35.473
Cadets!

08:35.556 --> 08:36.682
Fall in!

08:36.933 --> 08:39.685
Face the platform!

08:39.769 --> 08:44.941
No one has persuaded me
to risk my life either.

08:45.942 --> 08:50.321
This is the time
when the decision has to be all mine.

08:58.704 --> 09:02.708
I am Commander Erwin Smith
of the Scout Regiment.

09:04.001 --> 09:06.128
Today, you are going to choose
a regiment to join.

09:06.712 --> 09:11.342
To put it bluntly, this is my invitation
for you to join the Scouts.

09:11.926 --> 09:14.011
I am sure that,
after this recent Titan attack,

09:14.554 --> 09:17.390
you've already come to know their horror,

09:17.723 --> 09:20.685
as well as the limits
of your own abilities.

09:21.269 --> 09:22.228
However,

09:22.979 --> 09:24.522
through this battle,

09:24.605 --> 09:27.400
humanity has gained an unprecedented
advancement toward victory.

09:28.276 --> 09:30.194
I'm referring to Eren Jaeger.

09:31.737 --> 09:34.532
He has proven, by risking life and limb,

09:35.074 --> 09:37.868
that he is unquestionably on our side.

09:40.496 --> 09:45.543
What's more, he has helped us
not only foil the Titans' invasion,

09:46.127 --> 09:49.338
but also gave us a way
to learn the truth behind the Titans!

09:55.344 --> 09:56.470
We have a reason to believe that

09:56.554 --> 09:58.222
the basement of his home
in Shiganshina District

09:58.514 --> 10:01.058
houses a secret of the Titans
that not even he is aware of.

10:01.851 --> 10:04.353
If we can just reach this basement,

10:05.104 --> 10:07.231
we may be able to obtain information

10:07.315 --> 10:11.110
that will help us break free
from the Titans' century-long tyranny.

10:13.279 --> 10:14.614
Basement?

10:15.615 --> 10:17.491
Things have already progressed this far?

10:18.200 --> 10:20.911
If we can figure out what the Titans are,
we can turn the tables on them!

10:22.121 --> 10:27.126
However badly he wants new recruits,
going public with this is too much.

10:27.960 --> 10:30.630
Or is this a part of some sort of plan?

10:31.380 --> 10:35.176
Just what does the Commander want?

10:39.055 --> 10:42.183
We will head for the basement
in Shiganshina District.

10:43.267 --> 10:47.021
However, doing so
will require taking back Wall Maria.

10:47.396 --> 10:50.358
In other words,
our goal is the same as it's always been.

10:51.942 --> 10:54.862
But now that Trost District's gate
is unusable,

10:55.613 --> 10:58.366
we have no choice but to depart from
Calaneth District, further to the east.

10:59.992 --> 11:04.997
The entire battalion route we spent
four years establishing is now useless.

11:07.625 --> 11:10.961
During those four years,
over 60 percent of the Scouts died.

11:12.129 --> 11:13.631
Sixty percent in four years.

11:14.757 --> 11:16.592
Truly unbelievable numbers.

11:19.136 --> 11:21.764
In one month, there will be
an Exterior Scouting Mission.

11:21.847 --> 11:23.682
New recruits from your class
will take part in it,

11:24.308 --> 11:27.103
of which I estimate 30 percent will die.

11:28.062 --> 11:30.272
And in four years, most will be dead.

11:30.856 --> 11:33.651
However, whoever prevails

11:33.901 --> 11:36.904
will become a highly-skilled soldier
who can survive anything.

11:41.700 --> 11:43.661
Knowing this dismal state of affairs,

11:44.328 --> 11:47.039
whoever still wishes
to put their life on the line,

11:47.248 --> 11:48.541
remain here.

11:49.542 --> 11:56.215
Ask yourself if you can give your heart
for the sake of humankind!

12:01.804 --> 12:02.805
That is all.

12:03.347 --> 12:05.683
Those who wish to join
other regiments may leave.

12:08.352 --> 12:09.270
Sir!

12:09.937 --> 12:12.231
Don't you think
that was overly intimidating?

12:12.815 --> 12:14.358
No one is going to stay behind now!

12:39.800 --> 12:40.885
Damn it.

12:41.218 --> 12:43.971
Please, I've already decided!

12:44.889 --> 12:47.975
Don't make me hate myself
any more than this!

12:49.059 --> 12:52.813
If I don't walk away now,
I'll have to go through that again!

12:54.398 --> 12:57.943
I originally left my village
to join the Military Police Regiment.

12:59.361 --> 13:00.863
Mom will be so happy.

13:01.113 --> 13:04.783
And if I join it,
everyone will finally respect me too.

13:05.826 --> 13:07.828
But now we know it.

13:08.787 --> 13:10.664
Now we've seen it.

13:11.290 --> 13:12.958
How the Titans...

13:13.959 --> 13:15.586
Eat people!

13:40.819 --> 13:44.823
If you cadets were told to die, could you?

13:45.407 --> 13:46.742
We don't wish to die, sir!

13:48.661 --> 13:49.537
I see.

13:50.162 --> 13:51.747
You each have an outstanding look on you.

13:54.166 --> 13:56.710
All of you here are hereby accepted

13:56.794 --> 13:59.171
as new members of the Scout Regiment!

13:59.755 --> 14:01.632
This is a genuine salute!

14:02.132 --> 14:03.801
Give your hearts!

14:05.469 --> 14:06.428
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

14:09.807 --> 14:10.808
Everyone...

14:12.017 --> 14:13.227
Joining the Scout Regiment?

14:13.310 --> 14:14.687
Man, this sucks.

14:15.896 --> 14:17.064
I'm scared!

14:17.147 --> 14:18.566
I want to go home!

14:18.649 --> 14:21.068
I don't care anymore.

14:25.155 --> 14:27.825
If you're going to cry, then don't stay.

14:29.910 --> 14:31.704
You've done well to endure your fear.

14:32.246 --> 14:34.290
You're all brave soldiers.

14:35.332 --> 14:37.084
I respect you from the bottom of my heart.

14:45.509 --> 14:46.510
Salute!

14:48.220 --> 14:50.055
I'm Squad Leader Ness.

14:50.472 --> 14:52.433
And this is my horse, Charrete.

14:52.683 --> 14:57.271
Charrete likes to pull hair,
so watch out if you don't want to go bald.

14:57.688 --> 14:58.689
It's nice to meet you.

14:59.982 --> 15:01.984
You idiot! Stop that, Charrete!

15:02.484 --> 15:04.570
Someone, do something! Hey!

15:04.653 --> 15:06.572
Our training began the next day.

15:07.031 --> 15:09.491
However, it was focused less
on actual combat

15:09.575 --> 15:12.870
and more on having Commander Erwin's
Long-Range Scouting Formation

15:12.953 --> 15:14.246
drummed into our heads.

15:15.247 --> 15:18.792
Oddly enough, although it was
a precise, calculated formation,

15:19.168 --> 15:22.922
Eren Jaeger's position
was nowhere to be found.

15:23.756 --> 15:25.507
You rookies will be here,

15:25.966 --> 15:29.386
between the cart guard team
and the scout support team.

15:29.762 --> 15:33.057
Here, you will run alongside spare horses
and relay signals.

15:34.475 --> 15:36.936
Our Special Operations Squad
will be positioned here,

15:37.478 --> 15:39.104
on standby at the rear of the center rank.

15:39.605 --> 15:41.190
That's pretty far back.

15:41.941 --> 15:44.193
This is the safest position
in the formation.

15:44.652 --> 15:47.738
Not even the supply wagons
get this level of treatment.

15:48.405 --> 15:51.325
Our goal this time is simply
to leave and come back though.

15:52.159 --> 15:54.662
This expedition is meant to be short,
as it's also a test run

15:55.204 --> 15:58.624
to see if we can get you all the way
to Shiganshina District or not.

15:59.833 --> 16:00.751
Well...

16:01.085 --> 16:05.589
I still don't know what to do
with this ability of mine.

16:06.256 --> 16:09.802
Do you understand
what the Commander asked you back then?

16:09.885 --> 16:10.761
What?

16:11.762 --> 16:13.347
What do you think the enemy is?

16:13.764 --> 16:16.016
Do any of you know what he meant?

16:16.100 --> 16:17.101
No.

16:18.185 --> 16:21.313
I would be lying
if I said I understood it all.

16:21.605 --> 16:24.024
- But I--
- It's possible

16:24.233 --> 16:26.235
that there's another goal
to this operation.

16:26.610 --> 16:30.990
But the Commander decided that there's
no need to explain to the soldiers.

16:31.281 --> 16:35.744
So we should just focus
on leaving and coming back.

16:36.787 --> 16:37.871
Have faith in the Commander.

16:38.122 --> 16:38.998
Yes, sir.

16:39.707 --> 16:41.000
That's all for today's training.

16:41.291 --> 16:42.334
Prepare to head back.

16:58.600 --> 16:59.435
Oh, it's them!

16:59.727 --> 17:03.105
Oruo, may I go talk with my classmates
for a minute?

17:03.188 --> 17:05.065
Go on.

17:05.274 --> 17:06.108
Hey! Mikasa!

17:06.191 --> 17:07.026
Armin!

17:08.485 --> 17:09.319
Eren!

17:09.778 --> 17:11.864
It feels like it's been forever!

17:12.031 --> 17:12.906
Eren.

17:13.449 --> 17:15.159
Have they mistreated you in any way?

17:15.576 --> 17:17.745
Like studying and examining
every bit of you

17:18.078 --> 17:19.872
or putting you through mental torture?

17:19.997 --> 17:22.041
No, not at all.

17:22.833 --> 17:24.710
That pipsqueak went way too far.

17:25.252 --> 17:27.212
I will make him pay someday.

17:27.296 --> 17:30.007
Are you talking about Captain Levi?

17:30.674 --> 17:31.884
Hey, Eren!

17:31.967 --> 17:33.260
Long time, no see!

17:33.343 --> 17:36.388
Oh, my goodness! You're all here?

17:37.681 --> 17:38.599
But...

17:39.058 --> 17:40.934
If you're here,

17:41.351 --> 17:43.437
does that mean you joined
the Scout Regiment?

17:43.645 --> 17:45.689
Why else would we be here?

17:46.106 --> 17:50.778
Then just Jean, Annie, and Marco joined
the Military Police Regiment?

17:54.448 --> 17:55.407
Wait.

17:55.574 --> 17:56.575
You too?

17:57.242 --> 17:58.368
Marco is dead.

17:58.577 --> 17:59.411
What?

18:00.204 --> 18:02.289
What did you just say?

18:03.499 --> 18:06.210
Did you say Marco is dead?

18:07.419 --> 18:10.714
Apparently, not everyone can die
in a dramatic way.

18:11.298 --> 18:13.675
I don't even know how he went down.

18:14.927 --> 18:18.639
He died all alone,
without anyone knowing or seeing him.

18:19.389 --> 18:20.432
Marco did...

18:23.644 --> 18:25.646
Hey! Gather around, rookies!

18:26.855 --> 18:28.565
Your uniforms are here!

19:07.437 --> 19:09.356
Are you guys really...

19:09.940 --> 19:10.774
Yes.

19:10.858 --> 19:13.277
We're taking part
in the upcoming operation too.

19:13.777 --> 19:14.736
Hey, Eren.

19:15.195 --> 19:18.907
I heard you tried to kill Mikasa
when you turned into a Titan.

19:19.533 --> 19:21.118
What was all that about?

19:21.785 --> 19:24.246
It's not like that.
He was swatting at a fly.

19:24.329 --> 19:25.747
I'm not asking you.

19:27.166 --> 19:28.292
Actually, Mikasa,

19:28.750 --> 19:31.003
that cut on your cheek looks pretty deep.

19:32.171 --> 19:33.755
When did you get it?

19:36.842 --> 19:38.093
Apparently, it's true.

19:38.552 --> 19:41.471
I tried to kill Mikasa
when I was in Titan form.

19:41.555 --> 19:42.723
Apparently?

19:42.806 --> 19:44.391
Meaning, you don't remember?

19:44.766 --> 19:48.437
So basically, you never knew about
this Titan ability of yours until now

19:48.979 --> 19:51.899
and you don't have full control over it?

19:52.191 --> 19:54.067
Yes. That's right.

19:58.405 --> 19:59.698
Did you hear that, guys?

19:59.781 --> 20:01.325
Sounds like this is the current situation.

20:01.909 --> 20:04.745
Our lives and the lives of all humankind
rest on his shoulders.

20:05.329 --> 20:09.499
We'll probably end up like Marco too,
dead before Eren knows it.

20:10.083 --> 20:13.795
Jean, what's the point
in chastising Eren now?

20:14.922 --> 20:16.340
You know, Mikasa,

20:17.007 --> 20:22.387
not everyone is willing to needlessly die
for Eren like you.

20:23.513 --> 20:28.977
We should know
what we're laying down our lives for.

20:29.603 --> 20:32.898
Otherwise, we'll end up hesitating
when the time comes.

20:33.440 --> 20:36.276
We're asking Eren for a guarantee.

20:37.486 --> 20:39.696
Show us what you're worth,

20:40.822 --> 20:44.409
so we can see
if our lives are worth as much.

20:49.164 --> 20:50.540
So Eren...

20:51.625 --> 20:55.587
We're really counting on you, you hear?

20:57.422 --> 20:58.423
Yes.

21:05.472 --> 21:07.099
Commander, it's almost time.

21:09.268 --> 21:11.603
We've lured the nearby Titans away!

21:12.271 --> 21:14.064
Thirty seconds to gate opening!

21:21.446 --> 21:22.781
It's the Scouts!

21:23.156 --> 21:26.410
The marks on their backs
are called the Wings of Freedom!

21:26.576 --> 21:27.953
That's so cool!

21:29.538 --> 21:30.580
This is it!

21:31.623 --> 21:34.751
Humanity is now about
to take another step forward!

21:35.544 --> 21:38.380
Show us what you're made of!

21:40.590 --> 21:42.009
Open the gate!

21:54.730 --> 21:56.315
Forward!

22:01.236 --> 22:04.406
Now commencing
the 57th Exterior Scouting Mission!

22:05.490 --> 22:07.242
Move out!

23:42.921 --> 23:45.382
The Scout Regiment takes up
its Long-Range Scouting Formation

23:45.674 --> 23:48.135
and makes progress beyond the wall.

23:48.802 --> 23:51.138
Suddenly, they encounter

23:51.555 --> 23:54.599
a mysterious, intelligent Titan.
